# Extension UI

Use the browser's own features before writing script.

- Put fields that are submitted together in a `<form>`, with a submit button, so Enter works.
- Use constraint validation (`required`, `minlength`, `type`, `reportValidity`) instead of hand-written checks and status text.
- Use `autocomplete` so Firefox can generate and fill passwords. Do not store the passphrase.
- Buttons that do not submit the form stay `type="button"`.
- Download, notifications, context menus, and clipboard stay on the WebExtension APIs.

Script remains for cryptography, signing requests, fetching media, and storage. Do not reimplement those with a library.
